Design.md:- **`audigma-dsp`**: Pure numerical processing (`no_std`-friendly core logic, zero OS/file/network I/O). Implements domain rate/format types (`PcmRateHz`, `DsdBitRateHz`, `TransportFrameRateHz`), `DspConfiguration`, built-in verified filter and modulator coefficient tables (`presets.rs`: `PRESET_BALANCED`, `PRESET_REFERENCE`, `PRESET_LOW_LATENCY`), polyphase & half-band FIR interpolation, state-space / CRFB delta-sigma modulators, TPDF dither, overload guards, and thread-level hardware subnormal flushing (FTZ/DAZ). Portable across any operating system.
Design.md:- **Hardware FTZ/DAZ:** Inside the 1-bit DSM loop, feedback is strictly `{-1.0, +1.0}`, keeping integrators excited. However, upstream PCM FIR/IIR stages fed digital silence can decay into subnormal floats and cause severe CPU tail-latency spikes. Every DSP worker thread sets hardware **Flush-To-Zero (FTZ)** and **Denormals-Are-Zero (DAZ)** (`MXCSR` on `x86_64`, `FPCR` on `aarch64`) on thread entry.
